+# Daily Grind performance audit
+
+## Scope and evidence
+
+Audited the complete repository: a single static `index.html`, inline CSS, one
+remote stock photograph, and `package.json`. There is no application JavaScript,
+API, font download, framework, build pipeline, or implementation of the linked
+routes in this repository.
+
+Verification was limited to source analysis, image downloads, binary metadata,
+and static assertions. No browser, dev/preview server, server entrypoint, or
+start script was used. A build is unnecessary for this static HTML site.
+LCP, INP, CLS, TTFB, and Lighthouse scores were **not measured**. The changes
+address identified causes and risks; byte savings are measured file sizes,
+not claims of measured Core Web Vitals improvements.
+
+## Findings and changes
+
+| Area | Finding | Implementation / disposition |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| LCP discovery | Hero URL was only available inside CSS, without a priority hint. | A native HTML `picture` exposes the image to the preload scanner; its `img` uses `fetchpriority="high"` and eager loading. Only this image has elevated priority. |
+| Image transfer | All devices fetched the same 1350-pixel JPEG from Unsplash. | Local AVIF and WebP sources have 480, 768, 1280, and 1920-pixel variants; JPEG remains the fallback. The browser downloads one supported candidate. |
+| Responsive cover sizing | A portrait hero crops a landscape photograph, requiring more source pixels than its CSS width alone implies. | `sizes="max(100vw, 90vh, 30rem)"` accounts for full viewport width, the 3:2 image covering a 60vh hero, and the 20rem minimum hero height. `90vh` is a conservative estimate where `svh` is smaller. |
+| External connection | The photo required a second origin's DNS/TLS connection and availability. | All rendering assets are now same-origin, with content hashes in their filenames. |
+| Layout stability | A fixed 60vh hero could overflow with wrapped or enlarged text. | The hero reserves a minimum height before the image loads, grows for content, and uses `svh` with a `vh` fallback. The positioned image has explicit intrinsic dimensions and cannot move content on arrival. |
+| Mobile interactions | Navigation used an unwrapped flex row; grid columns had a 250px minimum even when less space was available. | Navigation wraps with CSS, small-screen link padding provides larger hit areas, and grid columns can shrink to the available width. All 13 link destinations are preserved. |
+| INP / main thread | No JavaScript handlers, long tasks, hydration, polling, layout-read loops, or third-party scripts exist in the supplied page. | Retained native navigation and zero JavaScript. No timer, worker, library, or speculative prefetch added. Destination response times cannot be assessed here. |
+| CSS / fonts | Small inline styles and system fonts already avoid stylesheet/font request chains. | Retained both; added no external styles, fonts, or frameworks. |
+| Rendering overhead | Three simple cards do not justify containment or deferred rendering. | No `content-visibility`, broad `will-change`, or service worker added. |
+| Input feedback | Focus visibility depended on browser defaults; color transitions ignored motion preference. | Added explicit keyboard focus outlines and a reduced-motion override. |
+
+The original photograph and centered dark-overlay treatment are retained. The
+image is decorative (`alt=""`), matching its previous CSS background semantics.
+No preload is needed: the picture is early in this small HTML document, and a
+separate preload could fetch a second format or wrong responsive candidate.
+
+## Payload evidence
+
+The original URL returned a **157,974-byte JPEG** during this audit. Sizes below
+are actual optimized file sizes, before HTTP compression:
+
+| Width | AVIF bytes | WebP bytes | AVIF reduction against original |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 480 | 12,965 | 25,812 | 91.8% |
+| 768 | 21,135 | 50,650 | 86.6% |
+| 1280 | 39,023 | 111,100 | 75.3% |
+| 1920 | 65,385 | 275,922 | 58.6% |
+
+The 1280px JPEG fallback is 142,732 bytes. The 1920px WebP provides greater
+resolution than the original and costs more bytes; it is only eligible for
+browsers without AVIF support when their viewport/density needs that size.
+Actual selection depends on viewport, pixel density, support, and browser
+heuristics; a phone does not necessarily select the smallest candidate.
+
+HTML grew from **4,708 to 6,295 bytes**, or **1,726 to 2,227 bytes with gzip**
+computed locally. The 501-byte gzip increase supplies responsive markup and
+layout fixes. For the 1280px AVIF example, combined gzipped HTML and image bytes
+fall from 159,700 to 41,250 (74.2%). This is a size comparison, not a timing
+measurement or confirmation that production serves gzip.
+
+The initial resource set remains HTML plus one photo. Rendering origins fall
+from two to one. All nine image variants together occupy disk space, but are
+not all fetched by a visitor.
+
+## Static verification completed
+
+- All 13 anchor destinations match the original document, in the same order.
+- Every referenced image exists, and no image asset is unreferenced.
+- Every filename's hash matches its file's SHA-256 prefix.
+- AVIF, WebP, and JPEG signatures are valid; WebP VP8X widths match descriptors.
+- Each modern source has four width candidates and an explicit cover-aware `sizes`.
+- Exactly one image is high priority, eagerly loaded, and explicitly dimensioned.
+- Every AVIF variant is under the 70,000-byte audit budget.
+- HTML has no scripts, remote resource URLs, or CSS `@import` chains.
+- `git diff --check` passes.
+
+These checks cannot verify decoded appearance, actual browser selection,
+interactive paint latency, or rendered layout. No visual verification was
+performed, as requested.
+
+## Deployment and measurement follow-up
+
+The repository has no deployment configuration or production URL. The following
+items require the actual host and are not represented as completed fixes:
+
+1. Serve hashed `/assets/coffee-*` files with
+   `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`. Serve HTML with
+   `Cache-Control: no-cache` so updates revalidate. Use the host's appropriate
+   configuration; no speculative host-specific file was added.
+2. Enable Brotli or gzip for HTML and correct image MIME types. Do not expect
+   meaningful additional compression from compressing AVIF/WebP/JPEG again.
+3. Check document TTFB, CDN delivery, redirects, and cache hits in production.
+4. Verify the linked destinations on the deployed service. `/menu`, account,
+   logout, ordering, and other linked routes are absent from this repository;
+   their latency and behavior remain outside this audit's code coverage.
+5. After deployment, use available CrUX/PageSpeed Insights field data or the
+   site's existing RUM to evaluate mobile and desktop separately. Target the
+   75th percentile: LCP ≤2.5s, INP ≤200ms, CLS ≤0.1. New field results need a
+   collection window; do not infer a passing score from the payload savings.
+
+## Image provenance and references
+
+All variants derive from the existing [Unsplash photograph](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085).
+They were downloaded using the image endpoint's explicit `fm`, `w`, `h`,
+`fit=crop`, and `q` parameters: quality 50 for AVIF, 72 for WebP, and 75 for JPEG.
+No generated images were used.
+
+Implementation guidance: [web.dev: Optimize LCP](https://web.dev/articles/optimize-lcp),
+[MDN: Responsive images](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Guides/Responsive_images),
+and the local modern-web-guidance `performance` and `optimize-image-priority`
+guides. These support early image discovery, responsive sources, reserved
+geometry, and prioritizing the hero without lazy loading it.
